    notes: 'JCM537 explicitly prepares and dispenses its salt/yeast/casein-peptone
      base before separate stock injections. Source transcription basis (literal input
      amounts, not calculated stock concentrations): Distilled water: 1 L; Yeast extract:
      4 g; NaCl: 1 g; CaCl2・2H2O: 0.1 g; KH2PO4: 0.2 g; NH4Cl: 0.3 g; Resazurin: 0.5
      mg; MgCl2・6H2O: 0.4 g; KCl: 0.5 g; Na2SO4: 0.15 g; Peptone from casein: 2 g.
      No batch-to-final-volume conversion is made. Handling atmosphere is not listed
      as a material part; pH reagents are source inputs, without an assertion of unchanged
      molecular species after pH adjustment. Nested formulations remain source-qualified
      named parts where exact composition/owner identity is not established. No verified
      exact eligible ontology term or existing whole-preparation owner was established
      by the bounded source/owner review. This self-registry mapping represents the
      preparation, not its individual constituents.'
